triage: fix_game: Two independent tests show the follow poll offering too few cards. In one a seat with no club is denied the Jack of Hearts when Baste is led; in the other a seat void in the led suit is denied a trump. That is a bug in the legality filter, not in the rules. The trump test also got Spades (1) stored where Hearts (3) was expected, which points to the declaration options or how the chosen option is turned into `trump`.
step C: building the game file
triage: fix_game: Each attempt failed on a different coder mistake: bookkeeping fields shown to players, a list comprehension using range (not an allowed function), reading `you` outside a per-player context, and extra constant attributes that no step ever changes. None of these comes from the rules, which the engine can express with flat steps, `when` conditions and simultaneous polls.
step C: building the game file
step D: evaluating
triage: fix_game: All three failures point at what the game offers and records during the declaration and the follow. The Taker's trump choice did not end up as the intended suit: the move actually played was the first option, 'Spades, partner seat 1', which suggests the scripted Hearts declaration was not among the options as offered. A seat that should be free to play any card (void in the led suit, with Spadille and Baste counted only as trump) was never offered that card. The rules are clear and expressible, so the file's option building and legality filter are at fault.
